tcc port for AdventOS — Phase 1 foundation
============================================

This directory is a vendored copy of TinyCC (mob branch, version
0.9.28rc) from https://repo.or.cz/tinycc.git, stripped down to the
i386 + ELF subset we need.

Files removed from upstream (Phase 1 trim):
  arm-*.c / arm-*.h            — ARM backend
  arm64-*.c / arm64-*.h        — ARM64 backend
  c67-*.c / c67-*.h            — TI C67 DSP backend
  riscv64-*.c / riscv64-*.h    — RISC-V backend
  x86_64-*.c / x86_64-*.h      — x86_64 backend
  il-gen.c, il-opcodes.h       — .NET IL backend
  coff.h                       — COFF format
  tcccoff.c                    — TI C67 COFF output
  tccpe.c                      — Windows PE/COFF output
  tccmacho.c                   — Apple Mach-O output
  win32/                       — Windows port
  tests/                       — 1.2 MB test corpus (out of scope)
  tcc-doc.texi, config.texi    — texinfo docs (need makeinfo)

What remains (~22 .c/.h files, ~1.8 MB):
  Core:
    tcc.c, tcc.h, libtcc.c, libtcc.h, tcclib.h
    tccpp.c    — preprocessor
    tccgen.c   — code generation (the big one, 275K)
    tccelf.c   — ELF output (141K)
    tccasm.c   — inline assembly
    tccdbg.c   — debug info (DWARF/stabs)
    tccrun.c   — `-run` mode (jit + relocate-and-jump)
    tcctools.c — `ar`, `strip` subcommands
    conftest.c — host autoconf probe
  i386 backend:
    i386-gen.c, i386-link.c, i386-asm.c
    i386-asm.h, i386-tok.h
  Shared headers:
    elf.h, dwarf.h, stab.h, tcctok.h
  Subtrees:
    include/ — tcc-shipped C headers (stddef.h, stdarg.h, tccdefs.h)
    lib/     — libtcc1 runtime helpers (64-bit shifts, soft-float, etc.)
    examples/

Status: Phase 1 — vendored + host-buildable. Not running in AdventOS
yet.

==============================================================
Phase 2 work plan (next session) — get tcc.elf running inside AdventOS
==============================================================

Goal: `cc /hello.c -o /hello.elf` inside AdventOS works with tcc.

Steps:

1. Cross-compile tcc with the AdventOS user toolchain
   (gcc -m32 -ffreestanding -nostdlib -nostartfiles ...).

2. Provide the libc surface tcc needs. Audited from upstream:

    From <stdio.h>:
       fopen, fclose, fread, fwrite, fputs, fputc, fseek, ftell,
       fprintf, sprintf, snprintf, ferror, feof, remove
    From <stdlib.h>:
       malloc, calloc, realloc, free, exit, abort, atoi, strtol,
       strtoll, getenv, qsort, system
    From <string.h>:
       strlen, strcpy, strncpy, strcat, strncat, strcmp, strncmp,
       strchr, strrchr, strstr, memcpy, memmove, memset, memcmp,
       strdup, strerror
    From <ctype.h>:
       isdigit, isalnum, isalpha, isspace, isupper, islower, isxdigit,
       tolower, toupper
    From <errno.h>:
       errno (TLS-ish global; just a global int for cc)
    From <setjmp.h>:
       setjmp, longjmp  (used by -run mode error recovery; can stub)
    From <unistd.h>:
       getcwd, unlink, access, sysconf
    From <fcntl.h>:
       O_RDONLY etc. macros (just defines)
    From <sys/stat.h>:
       struct stat, stat (used to check file existence)
    From <time.h>:
       time(NULL) for the predefined __DATE__ / __TIME__ macros

   libuser already provides: malloc, free, memcpy, memset, strlen,
   strcmp, atoi, printf, exit (via sys_exit). The rest need
   implementation — see [`docs/116-pathB-tcc-foundation.md`] for the
   per-function size estimate (most are ~20-line wrappers around
   existing syscalls).

3. Patch tcc's ELF output stage (tccelf.c) so emitted binaries match
   AdventOS's format:
   - entry VA = 0x40000000 (not 0x08048000 / Linux default)
   - single PT_LOAD segment, no PT_DYNAMIC / PT_INTERP
   - no dynamic symbol table, no GOT/PLT
   The kernel's elf.c loader only honours PT_LOAD and maps it RWX;
   anything else is ignored. tcc's --static + -Wl,-Ttext=0x40000000
   gets close but still emits dynamic-link plumbing.

4. Ensure tcc-emitted binaries pick up start.o (provides _start that
   calls main). Either link start.o by default in tcc's driver, or
   inject the _start prologue into tcc's libtcc1 runtime.

5. Provide tcc's runtime helpers (libtcc1) as a static archive that
   AdventOS-compiled programs can link against.  tcc emits calls to
   __divdi3, __moddi3, etc. for 64-bit arithmetic on i386.

6. Smoke test: run tcc.elf inside AdventOS on a small program,
   verify the output is a runnable cap.elf-style binary.

7. Doc + ship.

==============================================================
Why not just keep cc?
==============================================================

cc (AdventOS's from-scratch compiler) handles ~80% of real C in
~6000 lines. tcc adds: float/double, long long, full type system,
function-like macros, _Generic, designated initializers, VLAs,
inline assembly, and proper standards conformance. The tradeoff is
~50× more compiler code in the tree and a hard libc dependency.
Both compilers can coexist; cc stays as the always-works,
no-external-deps backstop.
